findings.description:
The new-test list covers classification completeness, routing and precedence, the checker rule, and `migrate-personal` happy and no-op paths. It has no automated test for:

- delete routing;
- the collision branches (different value, identical value);
- the per-key `failed: <error>` path and the "present in both files" recovery state;
- `cf init` gitignore handling (create, append, already present).

The parent architecture principle is "No behavior changes without tests". The failure modes at lines 149-151 are enumerated, but none has a test asserting its observable signal. Step 9 covers the collision manually only.
